dtlp: runs with its environment options unset.

dtlp runs under set -u and tests each option with ${#VAR}; ksh93 stops
there when the variable is unset ("LPDEST: parameter not set"), and the
print actions set none of them, so dtlp exited before its dialog. It
tests ${VAR-} instead. SINGLE_QUOTE, which quotes the banner title in
the lp command that dtlp evals, was never set: it is a single quote.

--- a/programs/dtprintegrate/dtlp.src
+++ b/programs/dtprintegrate/dtlp.src
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@
 XCOMM For string processing
 XCOMM
 MINUS_T="-t"
+SINGLE_QUOTE="'"
 
